Hi!

My second ascension, first spellcaster ascension. My other ascension was
back in version 3.3.1 about three years ago, and I haven't played a lot
since about a month ago. This was also my first and probably my last
character on alt.org, because the people I live with use up way to much
of our bandwith. Playing with a lag of nearly a second per move is
_very_ annoying. But, after loosing a Shao Pai Lon, a vegetarian,
weaponless monk on astral plane in a way that could've been avoided very
easily with my equipment, it's good to know I can still win this game. :)
This game was also the first time I got to the quest with a wizard. It's
amazing how powerful a wizard with the Eye of the Aethiopica becomes.
With the Eye, finger of death, magic missile, cone of cold, teleportitis
and teleport control, nothing could stand in my way.

The story as far as I remember:
Found an altar on first level, co-aligned it and sacced until I received
Magicbane. Made my (only) stash on level four, where I found another
altar. Sokoban contained an "oR, but I had already obtained one from a
shop in the second Dl (although it took me a while until I found out it
was one). Minetown lighting store had a magic lamp, but since I was torn
between wishing for SDSM or speed boots, I kept it as a light source
till the end of the game. An aleax in big room gave me Demonbane, which
I used as secondary weapon beside my +2 Magicbane. I had collected a
nice supply of elven daggers by this time, also. Got the identify-spell
somewhere around this time and got crowned shortly after. FoD started a
whopping 93% fail chance.
A few levels down I got teleportitis, but no TC, from a tengu. luckily I
had already found a cursed scroll of genocied, so I went back to Sokoban
and ordered more tengus. And immediately after that, I fainted of hunger.
When I woke up the tengus had reduced my HP to 2. Prayed. Weakness cured,
but still at 2HP. Went down, teleported away, and reached into my bag of
holding to get out my two blessed potions of full healing. After
quaffing one, the tengus were standing beside me again, and died soon
after. The last one finally gave me TC.
Proceeded down with way to high armor class. Was still somewhere around
AC 0 when I hit the castle, which nearly cost me my life when I met a
resident titan. And his 5 summoned dragons, his 4 summoned jabberwocks,
his summoned vampire lords... it was awful. I had to use the e-word to
get out of that mess. I really dislike using the e-word, it feels like
cheating every time I use it. Finally hit the titan with my FoD, though
still at 63% fail chance. The /oW was (0:1), and I wished for the usual
scrolls, SDSM, a pair of speed boots, a HoB and a T-Shirt. Although I
hadn't found a magic marker yet, I had enough scrolls of EA for the
magic stuff. Next target: Wizard quest. God, was that one easy. :)
With the Eye of the Aethiopica in my hands I stopped using the daggers,
and FoD'ed nearly every enemy with a high possibility to have a potion
of GL or FH and the ability to use it. Used Asmodeus to get to kill the
four lawful named demons, killed Juiblex in his lair, and went down to
Orcus. While Orcus did summon Yeenoghu, he refused to summon Demogorgon.
It was quite annoying waiting around Orcus with his spellcasting, so I
killed him. Well, I thought, maybe it's better not meeting Demogorgon in
this game, although I had prepared my gear for my first meeting with him.
Further down in Gehennom I found a magic marker, and wrote some more
scrolls of EA to improve my shield and gloves, wrote charging scrolls
with the rest of the charges. Lost protection AC due to praying too soon.
I was sure more turns had elapsed, one gets to the stash and back really
fast #invoking the Eye.
Dived down to the last level, marked the VS, went and death-ray'ed the
wizard. Molochs Sanctum was... interesting. At first it was really
annoying. Liches kept me running between the upstairs and the graveyard,
when suddenly a purple & showed up. Demogorgon appeared at last. Luckily,
I had cure sickness at 0% fail chance, so I slowly fought my way back to
the upstairs, curing sickness every few turns, claimed dominion over the
upstairs and dropped a scroll of scare monster. Some cones of cold later
Demogorgon was demoted to an ex-demon. But what did was it that he
dropped? The Amulet of Yendor! He stole it from the high priest! Wanted
to get a promotion, eh? Well, good for me, this way I did not need to
continue farther than the graveyard. And it would be a long way back up,
so I thought better than to clear out the rest of Molochs Sanctum,
remembering how annoying it was with the monk two weeks ago.
Climbing up again, I got thrown back only about six times. Rodney showed
up again three times on the way back up, always falling to my finger of
death without getting the chance to do anything. I love this spell.
Did I already mention how useful Magicbane is? With liches on the loose,
I got subjected to quite a lot of maligned auras in this game, but only
two of them were not absorbed by MB. In the plane of air I met an archon
with a Sunsword, which I claimed for me, my bag of holding and my score.=20
On Astral, I had to kill one arch-lich before proceeding. Left Altar was
Pestilence, middle Death and right one had Famine. I wanted to start
=66rom the right, but Death opened his door, so I began in the middle.
Altar was lawful, so I worked my way back down and to the right. On the
way to the next altar I avoided most enemies, and right altar proved to
be the one of Thoth. After shortly thinking about mopping up the enemies
that were hanging around I decided to #offer the amulet. Better safe
than sorry. ;)
Btw, no Ludios.

